      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Heart failure, arrhythmia, or chest pain can be a consequence of diabetes independent of coronary disease or hypertension. Diastolic myocardial dysfunction is common, contributing to the high mortality during acute infarction. The authors discuss diabetic cardiomyopathy and its management."},
